WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.486
SBOMs can strengthen vulnerability management by helping teams identify where affected components are used.

2
00:00:06.486 --> 00:00:13.011
When a vulnerability is disclosed, the first operational question is often whether the organization is exposed.

3
00:00:13.011 --> 00:00:21.801
Without component visibility, teams may need to search repositories, contact product owners, inspect builds, or wait for manual analysis.

4
00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:24.196
That can slow response when time matters.

5
00:00:24.196 --> 00:00:31.300
With usable SBOM data, teams can compare known vulnerable components and versions against software inventories.

6
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.457
This can help identify affected products, prioritize investigation, and focus remediation effort.

7
00:00:37.457 --> 00:00:44.680
SBOMs do not replace vulnerability scanning, patch management, secure coding, testing, or incident response.

8
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:50.078
They complement those activities by improving the quality and speed of component-level visibility.

9
00:00:50.078 --> 00:00:51.895
Context is still necessary.

10
00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:58.749
A component may be present but not reachable, not used in a vulnerable way, or protected by other controls.

11
00:00:58.749 --> 00:01:03.439
Teams still need analysis to determine actual exposure and response priority.

12
00:01:03.439 --> 00:01:07.290
SBOMs can also support long-term vulnerability trends.

13
00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:17.308
Organizations can see which products depend on outdated components, where unsupported libraries remain, and which teams may need help reducing dependency risk.

14
00:01:17.308 --> 00:01:31.127
The best vulnerability management use cases connect SBOMs to ownership, deployment data, severity information, exploitability analysis, remediation workflows, and verification that changes were completed.

15
00:01:31.127 --> 00:01:34.938
This connection is what turns inventory into response capability.

16
00:01:34.938 --> 00:01:44.766
An SBOM can show that a component exists, but ownership, deployment context, and remediation tracking help the organization decide what to do next.
